# The cron service's schedule, run by supercronic (see the compose
# `cron` service and the Dockerfile's pinned binary). One line per
# scheduled command; supercronic runs jobs independently, so lines
# never queue behind each other. Every command here must be safe to
# miss and safe to double (a pure age or idempotent judgement): the
# schedule is a tick, each command's own baseline is the guarantee.
# Times read on the container's clock, which is UTC (the image sets
# no TZ). supercronic parses this file at startup, so a schedule edit
# needs the cron service restarted (make restart-cron); the COMMANDS
# hot-reload regardless, since each tick imports off the bind mount.
0 * * * * uv run --frozen --package openbower-core python apps/core/manage.py prune_bench_runs
*/15 * * * * uv run --frozen --package openbower-core python apps/core/manage.py reclaim_node_runs
0 * * * * uv run --frozen --package openbower-core python apps/core/manage.py prune_webhook_deliveries
* * * * * uv run --frozen --package openbower-core python apps/core/manage.py flush_webhooks
